2. Find the Highest and Lowest Frequency elements in an Array :
    
Problem Statement: Given an array of size N. Find the highest and lowest frequency element.

Examples:

Example 1:
Input: array[] = {10,5,10,15,10,5};
Output: 10 15
Explanation: The frequency of 10 is 3, i.e. the highest and the frequency of 15 is 1 i.e. the lowest.


// Input: array[] = {10,5,10,15,10,5};
// Output: 10 15
// Explanation: The frequency of 10 is 3, i.e. the highest and the frequency of 15 is 1 i.e. the lowest.

import java.util.*;
public class Main{
    public static void main(String[] args){
        int arr[] = {10,5,10,15,10,5};
        boolean visited[] = new boolean[arr.length];
             int maxVal = -1;
            int minVal = -1;
            int maxFreq = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
            int minFreq = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        for(int i = 0; i<arr.length;i++){
            if(visited[i])
            continue;
            
            int count = 1;
            for(int j = i+1;j<arr.length;j++){
                if(arr[i] == arr[j]){
                    count++;
                    visited[j] = true;
                }
            }
            
            if(count>maxFreq){
              maxFreq = count;
              maxVal = arr[i];
          }
          
          if(count<minFreq){
              minFreq = count;
              minVal = arr[i];
          }
            
         
        }
          System.out.println("The highest frequency is" + maxVal + "which is" + maxFreq);
         System.out.print("The  Lowest frequency is" + minVal + "which is" + minFreq);
          
        
    }
}

Output:
The highest frequency element is: 10
The lowest frequency element is: 15
Time Complexity: O(N*N), where N = size of the array. We are using the nested loop to find the frequency.
Space Complexity:  O(N), where N = size of the array. It is for the visited array we are using.

